      "body": "## Motivation\nWhen the scheduler is paused (self._engine_paused = True), the event loops repeatedly poll non-blocking sockets and record metrics in a tight loop without waiting, which can spin CPU cores during pause states.\n\n## Modifications\n- In _record_scheduler_state_for_paused_engine, call maybe_sleep_on_idle() if an idle sleeper is configured.\n- Fall back to sleeping 5ms when an idle sleeper is not available.\n- Added \test_paused_engine_waits_or_throttles to \test/registered/unit/managers/test_scheduler_pause_generation.py.\n\n## Checklist\n- [x] Add unit tests according to the Run and add unit tests.\n\n<!-- pr-states:start -->\n---\n### CI States\n\nLatest PR Test (Base): <!-- slot:pr-test:start -->:x: [Run #41350119225](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/41350119225)<!-- slot:pr-test:end -->\nLatest PR Test (Extra): <!-- slot:pr-test-extra:start -->:x: [Run #41350119211](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/41350119211)<!-- slot:pr-test-extra:end -->\nLatest PR Test (AMD ROCm 10): <!-- slot:pr-test-amd:start -->:x: [Run #41350119124](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/41350119124)<!-- slot:pr-test-amd:end -->\n\n> [!TIP]\n> Base CI only covers the core cases, and its workload may not exercise your change. Use `/rerun-test` to run the tests your change touches, or copy this prompt for an agent:\n>\n> ```text\n> Find the registered tests this PR affects and run them with /rerun-test, following https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/blob/main/.agents/skills/rerun-test/SKILL.md\n> ```\n<!-- pr-states:end -->",
